# The emulator install is not the project. Ignore everything at the top level,
# then add back only what is actually authored here: the Lua tool, the analysis
# scripts, the engine notes, and the older script backups that predate git.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/scripts/
!/analysis/
!/run_vsav_training.bat
!/run_vsav_training.sh
!/training_modes.json
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
# Shipped in every release but authored upstream, so they were never in here -
# the zip carried them forward from the previous zip instead. That chain broke
# the moment the Downloads folder was cleared: the files existed nowhere else
# and a rebuild would have quietly dropped them. Tracked now.
!/handoff_VSAV_investigation.md
# Handoff notes are authored here and are the first thing a new session
# reads. Whitelisted by pattern so the next one does not have to remember
# to add itself - the last one was only tracked because someone noticed.
!/handoff_*.md
# Design notes, same reasoning and the same trap: design_action_pattern_library.md
# was written, committed with `git add -A`, and silently left untracked by the
# /* rule above. The commit message said it was in; git ls-files said otherwise.
# Whitelisted by pattern so the next one cannot repeat it.
!/design_*.md
!/run_vsav_training_flatpak.sh
!/vsav_training_flatpak.desktop
# Same story, found the hard way: these two are shipped in every zip but were
# never whitelisted, so the folder overwrite took them and git had no copy.
# Recovered from the v11.3.3 zip.
!/VSAV_TRAINING_v11.3.2_CHANGES.md
!/wakeup_reversal_behavior_v11.3.2.md
# Release notes live in the repo as well as on the page. Both languages.
!/RELEASE_NOTES.md
!/RELEASE_NOTES.ja.md
# The engine notes. The header above says these are authored here and belong in
# the repo, and they never were - 36 KB of measurements (the camera and its
# 16 px rule, the free-1 signature, $21 holding its value for one tick, the air
# dash at +8) existed on disk only. Every edit made to this file since it was
# created was never committed. Third time this class of miss has been found.
!/VSAV_MEMORY_NOTES.md

# Bulk data, at any depth. These stay on disk - reversal_logs_archive is the
# evidence base and must never be deleted (see analysis/archive_logs.py) - but
# it is 170 MB of traces and does not belong in history. mame_roms must not be
# committed at all.
reversal_logs/
reversal_logs_archive/
mame_code/
mame_roms/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Emulator working files that land inside the tracked directories.
*.fs
*.sav

# ツールが実行のたびに書き出す。設定そのものは履歴に残っているが、
# 以後の差分は追わない(2026-08-14 の指示)。
#
# Per-user state, not source. A used copy of this leaked into a release once,
# carrying a debugging configuration and the knockdown logger switched on.
#
# MATCH THE FAMILY, NOT ONE SPELLING. This listed the exact name, and a
# hand-made backup called training_settings_pre_action_patterns.json walked
# straight past it into the repo - 329 lines of the author's own configuration,
# found on the way to a release (2026-09-19).
training_settings*.json

# gen_max_steps.py parks the real settings here while a load test is loaded in
# their place. Same reason as above, and it must not be mistaken for source.
/analysis/training_settings.backup.json

# dashProbe.lua の出力。実測そのものは残す価値があるが、読み取った事実は
# VSAV_MEMORY_NOTES.md に書く。ログ自体は走らせるたびに増える。
/analysis/dash_probe.log
/analysis/select_probe.log
/analysis/lever_probe.log
/position_slide.log
# The emulator's working directory for a Lua script is scripts/, which is
# where the trace actually lands - and it must never reach a package.
/scripts/position_slide.log
/analysis/position_slide_*.log
# Frozen copies of the probe log. EVID-RUNTIME-001 cites one by SHA-256,
# so the live log has to stay free to grow while the cited copy stays put.
/analysis/dash_probe_*.log

# Release archives. The whitelist above already ignores them, but they kept
# turning up in the project folder next to the sources they were built from.
# Builds live outside the repo now (../../dist); this line is here so the
# intent is stated and not just an accident of the whitelist.
VSAV_Training_*.zip
scripts/action_pattern_trace.log

# The dated copies of the same thing. The port was abandoned and is being
# redesigned from the UI instead (design_action_pattern_library.md), so these
# sixteen files - one of them 49,912 lines, every name a dead end like
# eleventh_hook_dead - say nothing to anyone reading the published tree, which
# they reached on 2026-09-19.
#
# Dated probe logs that led somewhere stay tracked on purpose: the
# landing_predict ones are the evidence behind Auto (Landing).
analysis/action_pattern_trace_*.log
analysis/landing_predict_probe.log
# Measurement output, not authored here. Probe logs and the landing trace are
# produced by running the tool, run to hundreds of KB, and must never reach a
# release zip. Kept on disk so a past measurement can be re-read.
/analysis/archive/
/scripts/land_trace.log
